/**
\mainpage Escape API reference

Escape is a C++20 library for terminal output and typed input.
All public names are in the esc namespace.

- \ref esc::Terminal owns terminal modes, drawing, and input for a session.
- \ref esc::Output and \ref esc::Reader borrow streams for direct I/O.
- \ref esc::Parser decodes incremental byte input without I/O.
- \ref esc::Style and \ref esc::StylePatch describe appearance.
- \ref esc::TerminalProfile describes capability assumptions and fallback.
- \ref esc::GraphemeView and \ref esc::WidthPolicy support Unicode layout.

The namespace page lists free functions, command values, events, and color names.
Use the search box to find an overload or type. The repository's README and
`docs/tutorials.md` contain complete programs; `docs/behavior.md` explains
borrowing, validation, and restoration.
*/
